# Tests required for new features

Applies to **`mobile/`** (primary test suite) and **repo root** where tests exist or should be added.

## When tests are required

Add or extend automated tests in the **same PR** when you:

- Ship **new user-facing behavior** (views, buoy selection, history charts).
- Change **business rules** (parsing, conditions, cache/history retention, API routes in `server.ts`).
- Fix a **regression** — include a test that would have caught it.

Docs-only, comment-only, or dependency bumps with no logic change are exempt unless they alter runtime behavior.

## Where tests live

| Area | Runner | Location |
|------|--------|----------|
| Pure parsing / API helpers | Vitest | `mobile/src/lib/**/*.test.ts` |
| React components | Vitest + Testing Library | `mobile/src/**/*.test.tsx` |
| IndexedDB history | Vitest + fake-indexeddb | `mobile/src/lib/history-store.test.ts` |
| Dev port scripts | Node test runner | `mobile/scripts/*.test.mjs` |
| Full routes / navigation | Playwright | `mobile/e2e/*.spec.ts` |
| Root app / server | Manual + `pnpm build` | `src/**`, `server.ts` (add Vitest when logic grows) |

Run **`cd mobile && pnpm test`** for the mobile suite; **`pnpm test:pr`** before ship (**`feature-ship.mdc`**).

## Before ship / merge

- Run **scoped checks** from the table in **`feature-ship.mdc`** (match commands to changed paths).

## Do not

- Merge feature work with failing tests permanently skipped.
- Disable failing tests instead of fixing behavior.
